<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Falkland Islands</h1><p class="st-meta">1833 CE – present · capital Stanley</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British territory in the South Atlantic, settled by sheep farmers and claimed by Argentina as the Malvinas, which went to war over it in 1982.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> had established rival settlements in the islands in the 18th century. In the 1820s the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata</a> appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luis-vernet">Louis Vernet</a> as governor. In January 1833 a British warship expelled the Argentine garrison, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> took control. A crown colony was formed in 1841, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanley-falkland-islands">Stanley</a> became the capital in 1845.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The islands developed as a sheep-farming colony, much of it owned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falkland-islands-company">Falkland Islands Company</a>, with a small population of British descent. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanley-falkland-islands">Port Stanley</a> served ships rounding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-horn">Cape Horn</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentina</a> maintained its claim. On 2 April 1982 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina's</a> military government invaded; a British task force retook the islands, and Argentina surrendered on 14 June after a war that killed over 900 people.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Fishing licences from 1987 transformed the economy. In a 2013 referendum over 99 per cent of voters chose to stay British. The islands remain a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-overseas-territories">British Overseas Territory</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentina</a> still claims them.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/falkland-islands.jpg" alt="Falkland Islands" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Original: Government of the United Kingdom Vector: Nightstallion and Echando una mano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Falkland_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1833 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Stanley</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rex Hunt</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Malvinas, Colony of the Falkland Islands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=falkland-islands" aria-label="Falkland Islands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3373 3966 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Falkland Islands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3693 4222L4997 651M3693 4222L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3693 4222h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3693 4222h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Stanley. <a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=falkland-islands">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

